> f(x: u8) = 1 << x
> domain f
domain of f:
  x: u8, 0..255
  requires 0 <= x < 8  (shift amount; C UB otherwise)
  defined at 8 of 256 points
  defined for: 0..7
  undefined e.g. at x=8; x=9; x=10; x=11
  C undefined behaviour at 248 points, e.g. x=8
  over all 256 points of the domain
> range f
range of f -> u8:
  1..128   (8 distinct values)
  values: 1..2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128
  fits in u8
  undefined at 248 points
  over all 256 points of the domain
> wrap f
wrap analysis of f:
  1 << x   (u8)
      nuw holds
      nsw fails: signed wrap at 1 points, e.g. x=7
  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 55 points, e.g. x=8
      exact for: 0..7
  over all 256 points of the domain
> equiv f f
f and f are equal on the domain of f (exhaustive)
